From 5a55fada3f8356950498005f5351d9f1e8081031 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cyril Hrubis <metan@ucw.cz>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:32:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] select: unit: len2device_px rounded the size of a unit, not
 the length

css_unit_len2device_px() rounded px_per_unit to a whole device pixel
before multiplying by the length, the same way css_unit_len2css_px()
did for CSS pixels.  A unit is rarely a whole number of pixels: 1mm is
3.78px at 96dpi, so `width: 10mm` came out 40px from
css_computed_width_px(), where it is 37.8.

The product is now exact, and rounding is left to the caller, which
truncates the length it gets.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Cyril Hrubis <metan@ucw.cz>
---
 src/select/unit.c | 9 +++------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/select/unit.c b/src/select/unit.c
index 0a6697f..2fafb79 100644
--- a/src/select/unit.c
+++ b/src/select/unit.c
@@ -348,12 +348,9 @@ css_fixed css_unit_len2device_px(
 
 	px_per_unit = css_unit_css2device_px(px_per_unit, ctx->device_dpi);
 
-	/* Ensure we round px_per_unit to the nearest whole number of pixels:
-	 * the use of FIXTOINT() below will truncate. */
-	px_per_unit += F_0_5;
-
-	/* Calculate total number of pixels */
-	return FMUL(length, TRUNCATEFIX(px_per_unit));
+	/* Not rounded: a unit is rarely a whole number of device pixels, and
+	 * rounding it first made 10mm 40px at 96dpi, where it is 37.8. */
+	return FMUL(length, px_per_unit);
 }
 
